  "result": "I fixed the spurious notifications in `src/lib/mentions.ts`. `extractMentions` was scanning the whole comment body, code blocks included.\n\nThe file already had a `withoutCode` helper that blanks out fenced blocks and inline code spans, but nothing called it. `extractMentions` now runs the body through it first. So `@foo` inside a fenced block or backtick span no longer counts, and the same text outside code still does.\n\nI also made `withoutCode` a bit more robust while I was there. It now handles `~~~` fences as well as backtick fences, and a fence that is never closed is treated as running to the end of the comment.\n\nI ran `tests/lib/mentions.test.ts` and all 11 tests pass. I didn't add a test for the fenced-block case.\n\n`highlightMentions`, which styles mentions when a comment is displayed, still styles `@handle` text inside code blocks. That is visual only and doesn't trigger notifications, so I left it alone.",
